  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\integers.set]\nDeclares: Z := (\\naturals.set \\.set.cross./ \\naturals.set) \\.mod./ \\integer.equivalence is \\set\nDocumented:\n. called: \"integers\"\n. written: \"\\mathbb{Z}\"\n. description: \"The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ of integers, constructed as the quotient of\n                $\\mathbb{N} \\times \\mathbb{N}$ by the integer equivalence\n                relation. Each integer is a class of pairs $(n, m)$ representing\n                the difference $n - m$, so $\\mathbb{Z}$ contains the naturals\n                together with their negatives.\"\nId: \"2879813a-8202-4d27-b248-83687c132e84\"",
